the usual expectation for compilers is that the vtable pointer will be at the beginning of the struct, but CW PPC lays structs out in a very naive way

```
class Thing {
  int a;
  virtual void method();
  int b;
};
```

the vtable appears at the location of the first virtual method -- so this will place a at offset 0, the vtable at offset 4, and b at offset 8

that class would translate to ```
struct _Thing {
  int _a;
  void *__vt;
  int _b;
}``` instead of ```
struct _Thing {
  void *__vt;
  int _a;
  int _b;
};``` on cw

